                                                "sense_id": "4dbda61a-f1d2-3e0e-89ab-f491e18ac8e7",
                                                "text": "Directly combining in a low energy state (ground state) is less efficient, so these hydrogen atoms generally form with the electrons still in a high-energy state, and once combined, the electrons quickly release energy in the form of one or more photons as they transition to a low energy state. This release of photons is known as photon decoupling."
